1 WAIT
    The WAIT command waits for a time: a delta time, [dddd-]hh:mm:ss.cc.
    CTRL/Y or CTRL/C ends the wait.  WAIT leaves $STATUS alone.  Other
    processes (see HELP SPAWN) run while it waits.  In a subprocess SPAWN
    is waiting for, the keys go to the subprocess, so they end its WAIT
    (see HELP KEYS).

    Syntax:

        WAIT delta-time

    Example:

        $ WAIT 00:00:05
